Relevant tables / columns and why they matter  
• olist_orders.order_status : filter to keep only “delivered” orders.  
• olist_orders.order_delivered_customer_date : contains the delivery time‑stamp.  
  • substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)  → delivery year (YYYY).  
  • substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2) → delivery month (MM).  

Typical conditions that will be used  
• WHERE order_status = 'delivered'  
• AND substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')  

Below are ten exploratory‑to‑final SQLite queries (all capped with LIMIT 20) that progressively lead to the requested pivoted report.  
Each query is preceded by a brief comment.

```sql
-- 1) See all possible order_status values
SELECT DISTINCT order_status
FROM olist_orders
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Inspect the delivery years that actually appear in the data
SELECT DISTINCT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) AS delivery_year
FROM olist_orders
WHERE order_status = 'delivered'
ORDER BY delivery_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Count delivered orders per year (all years)
SELECT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)  AS delivery_year,
       COUNT(*)                                   AS delivered_orders
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
GROUP  BY delivery_year
ORDER  BY delivery_year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Check which months occurred in 2017 (sanity‑check)
SELECT DISTINCT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2) AS month_2017
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
  AND  substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) = '2017'
ORDER  BY month_2017
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Delivered orders per month for 2017 only
SELECT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2) AS month,
       COUNT(*)                                   AS orders_2017
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
  AND  substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) = '2017'
GROUP  BY month
ORDER  BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Delivered orders per month for 2016 only
SELECT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2) AS month,
       COUNT(*)                                   AS orders_2016
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
  AND  substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) = '2016'
GROUP  BY month
ORDER  BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Delivered orders per month for 2018 only
SELECT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2) AS month,
       COUNT(*)                                   AS orders_2018
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
  AND  substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) = '2018'
GROUP  BY month
ORDER  BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Long‑format counts (month, year, count) for 2016‑2018
SELECT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2) AS month,
       substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) AS year,
       COUNT(*)                                   AS delivered_orders
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
  AND  substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP  BY month, year
ORDER  BY month, year
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Pivoted counts using conditional aggregation (core idea)
SELECT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2)                              AS month,
       SUM(CASE WHEN substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)='2016' THEN 1 END) AS delivered_2016,
       SUM(CASE WHEN substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)='2017' THEN 1 END) AS delivered_2017,
       SUM(CASE WHEN substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)='2018' THEN 1 END) AS delivered_2018
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
  AND  substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP  BY month
ORDER  BY month
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Same as #9 but with month names and sorted numerically (final report)
SELECT substr(order_delivered_customer_date,6,2)                          AS month,
       SUM(CASE WHEN substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)='2016' THEN 1 END) AS "2016",
       SUM(CASE WHEN substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)='2017' THEN 1 END) AS "2017",
       SUM(CASE WHEN substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4)='2018' THEN 1 END) AS "2018"
FROM   olist_orders
WHERE  order_status = 'delivered'
  AND  substr(order_delivered_customer_date,1,4) IN ('2016','2017','2018')
GROUP  BY month
ORDER  BY CAST(month AS INTEGER)
LIMIT 20;
```

Running the last query (#10) will produce the requested report: each row = calendar month (01 … 12), each column = number of delivered orders in that month for 2016, 2017 and 2018 respectively.
